# Chaya navmesh fixture: a tiny real mesh in the CHAYA CANONICAL frame (metres, right-handed, +Z up).
# Used by tests/navmesh/test_recast_fixture.py, which runs the real Recast/Detour build (services/reconstruction/native/chaya-navmesh) over it.
#   floor      8 m x 4 m at z = 0
#   wall       x 3.9..4.1, y 0..2.6, 2.5 m tall: leaves a 1.4 m doorway at y 2.6..4.0 (plain geometry; Recast decides)
#   furniture  x 1.5..2.5, y 1.0..2.0, 0.9 m tall, in `g obstacle` (blocked geometry: never walkable)
#   wedge      x 6.2..7.2, y 0..1.2, rising 1.7 m over 1 m (59.5 degrees; plain geometry; Recast's slope test decides)
# Every face is wound counter-clockwise seen from outside (floor normal +Z).
